{"id": "unknown-2026-05-13-006", "date": "2026-05-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["uncertainty", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton retreats from multi-month highs on dollar pressure", "content": "ICE cotton futures ended mixed after Monday’s sharp rally, as a stronger US dollar triggered profit-booking despite bullish USDA supply-demand estimates.\nJuly 2026 cotton settled 1.65 per cent lower at 86.32 cents/lb, though volumes stayed exceptionally high.\nMarkets remained supported by tight supply expectations, while traders monitored US inflation, Fed outlook and US–China tariff uncertainty.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-retreats-from-multi-month-highs-on-dollar-pressure-310277-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "hm-2026-05-13-007", "date": "2026-05-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["hm"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "GFS 2026: Kering, H&M on putting sustainability back on the CFO agenda", "content": "Global Fashion Summit (GFS) 2026 highlighted the CFO’s growing role in embedding sustainability into fashion’s financial decision-making.\nAs earnings calls focus more on margins, AI and geopolitics, sustainability mentions have declined by about one-third since 2022.\nThe BCG-GFA report says CFOs must help prioritise, fund and measure circularity, EPR readiness and long-term resilience.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/gfs-2026-kering-h-m-on-putting-sustainability-back-on-the-cfo-agenda-310276-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-13-008", "date": "2026-05-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India captures Europe's apparel sourcing pivot", "content": "India has overtaken peers as Europe’s fastest-growing apparel supplier; EU-27 imports hit a record $6.96 billion in 2025, up 14.3 per cent YoY. \nQ1 surged 22.3 per cent, the strongest quarter in 4 years; home textiles climbed 18.6 per cent to $1.60 billion.\nThe zero-duty India-EU FTA wipes a 12 per cent tariff gap as Bangladesh logs 113 factory closures and Turkiye slides 11.3 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-captures-europe-s-apparel-sourcing-pivot-310273-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-13-009", "date": "2026-05-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Canada, Vietnam seek broader trade cooperation", "content": "Canada and Vietnam have agreed to further strengthen economic and trade ties as well as supply chain connectivity amid growing global uncertainties. \nThe issue was discussed at a meeting between Minister of Industry and Trade Le Manh Hung and Canadian ambassador to Vietnam Jim Nickel, who highlighted Vietnam’s growing role in global supply chains. \nThe two sides discussed talks on the ASEAN-Canada FTA. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/canada-vietnam-seek-broader-trade-cooperation-310269-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-13-010", "date": "2026-05-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s BGMEA, OS Hub sign MoU to strengthen apparel transparency", "content": "Bangladesh trade body BGMEA and US-based Open Supply Hub have signed an MoU to strengthen apparel sector transparency and digitally presenting factory information on the global supply chain platform.\nThe two sides will create an integrated digital database platform that will enable buyers to directly access information on the location, product categories and special capabilities of garment units.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-bgmea-os-hub-sign-mou-to-strengthen-apparel-transparency-310272-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
